A||N||21||Monkeyman||FedEx Sucks||||8||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||11-02-2001||06:06 PM||||Well, the morons at FedEx did it again.  I bought Old Lars' fiberglass headliner panel.  He shipped it out on 29 Oct.  I have a scan of the shipping receipt (thanx) that states that the delivery date should have been 31 Oct.  FedExs website said 1 Nov.  No problem so far.  Yesterday evening (when the package failed to arrive), I called FedEx.  I actually spoke with the same customer service representative that I had to deal with last time.  She tracked the package and said that it was still on it's way from Columbus, OH to Kokomo, IN (BTW--it left Columbus at 0022 yesterday am).  Said that the package should be here 1<sup>st</sup> thing this morning.  Since my wife is currently laid off, she spent the day at home just in case a delivery signature was needed.  I got home about 4pm to find no package.  I immediately called FedEx to find out where my package was.  (This is where the "fun" starts.)  Turns out that it's not really on it's way to Kokomo, but instead it was inadvertently shipped to Chicago (someone at FedEx really needs to invest in an atlas).  It <I>should</I>  arrive in Chicago tomorrow afternoon.  Customer service (poor choice of words for them) thinks it should arrive in Kokomo (nearest terminal to me) on Monday.  Hmmm...Last time this happened it took 2 1/2 days to get to Kokomo.  And another day and a half to get to me.  (For those of you who aren't interested enough to look at a map, it's about 200 miles from Chicago to Kokomo and another 30 miles back to here.)  Tonights customer rep even went as far as to suggest that the package might be lost as the package isn't showing up correctly on their computer.  Wonderful company, aren't they?  I hope nobody else has had the same problems with them.  (Maybe they just don't like me?)  <P>Thanx for letting me rant for a while.  (Old Lar--I'll email you once I find out what's really going on.)<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||8
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||11-02-2001||06:32 PM||||MM- sorry to hear that you're having such nasty trouble with FedEx.  I ship tons of stuff daily by FedEx and have only run into an issue once in the last 3 years (they split a multi-box shipment... stupid). BTW- are you using FedEx "Express" or FedEx "Ground" services?  'Cause they actually aren't the same system yet... FDX Ground is still running the old RPS system, and hasn't yet been integrated into the current "Express" system.  Just a thought.  Well, good luck to 'ya anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||11-02-2001||06:42 PM||||Both misdirected packages were shipped FedEx Ground.  I assumed that the merger had been completed years ago.  I'm glad that there are some that have shipped with FedEx without any problems.  I however, will never ship with them.  I'd rather pay a little more with UPS and feel certain that my package will arrive when it's supposed to.  (Knock on wood.  UPS hasn't failed me yet as far as on time deliveries go.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||11-02-2001||07:24 PM||||<B>UPDATE!!!!</B><P>I just got off the phone with FedEx (again).  As of 1:56pm today, my package is in...Sacramento, California!!  How did they miss Indiana?!?  I realize the Hoosier state isn't the largest state in the country, but it's a little tough to miss.  I'm guessing the "Welcome to Indiana" signs would have given it away.  This particular "customer service rep" (Dante Williams of KC, MO) said that "it must have been loaded on the wrong truck".  Umm...you bet it was.  Now the estimated delivery date is 8 Nov.  I'm guessing that they mean 2001.<P>Sorry to continue to rant, but this is getting ridiculous.  If anyone wants proof of this screw up, feel free to email me and I'd be happy to give you the tracking number so you can call FedEx directly.  (I certainly don't have anything to hide.)<P>News as it happens.  Film at 11.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Reality||11-02-2001||07:30 PM||||Sorry to hear about all the trouble. I have just one comment. Please don't ship my center console FedEx!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/realitysignature.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||11-02-2001||07:43 PM||||No chance of that, Reality.  I can walk your stuff to you faster than FedEx could get it to you.  Let's see...Wabash, IN to Athens, OH means that it has to go through Columbus, OH/Atlanta, GA/Milwaukee, WI/Portland, OR and London, England.  (In that order.)  Your stuff will be shipped UPS.  Unless you'd rather meet me halfway.  I'll email you about this when I send the pic of the ECM cover.||||reg||1
Z||000006||My7Fieros||11-03-2001||12:29 AM||||Sorry to hear that MM. I have to say though, you have got to be cursed or something lol. FedEx is by far the best in the business..I use them all the time and have never had a problem.<BR>Why am I so partial to FedEx? Well, first, they are based here in Memphis...this is where they started and where their home office is. Memphis is the busiest airport in the <B>world</B> every night from 9:00 pm to 9:00 am...due to FedEx planes. In fact Fred Smith lives about 3 miles away from me (and Oh my God you should see his house!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_dizzy.gif"> ).<BR>I have several family members that work for them, including my dad, and he does <B>very</B> well (you dont think I could afford 7 Fieros and a new Mustang on a cop's salary do you?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).<BR>Anyway sorry to ramble, but Ive kinda got a soft spot for "FredEx" as is called here. I rarely hear of them having shipping problems like the ones you've encountered. I was wondering, (sorry, but Ive never heard of that town you live in)..do you live on a rural route or anything like that? Ive heard of times when UPS and USPS have had late deliveries do to people that live "out in the boonies" (no offense if you do, hell I used to live outside Branson, MO!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> )<BR>Anyway, for some reason it kinda bothers me to hear people having bad expieriences w/FX.<BR>My dad is kinda a "big wig" there...send me a PM or an email if you like w/the whole story and all and I'll talk to him and see if something cant be done. Cant promise anything, but having connections can help sometimes!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/My7logo_1.gif"> ||||reg||9
Z||000007||Monkeyman||11-03-2001||01:13 AM||||Wabash has a population of about 20k so we're not small by any means (not that we're a thriving metropolis or anything, either  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ).  I've received around 30 packages from UPS in the past year and not one of them was delayed.  One got to me damaged, but that was all.  FedEx delivers in Wabash all the time.<P>It's not that they can't find the house.  The package that came from NY is now in CA!  Oops.  They didn't just miss my house, but my entire state!  I'm just plain disgusted.<P>I'll email you.  It doesn't matter if your father can get anything done or not.  It'll make me feel better knowing that someone in power at least knows what's going on.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Nashco||11-03-2001||03:45 AM||||In my experiences so far, shipping companies seem to vary based on location more than anything.  Where I'm at now, home and work, UPS is great, and on schedule within a couple minutes..it's amazing.  I've spent some time in Texas where the FedEx was the same way, almost perfectly timed.  The funny thing is, they both sucked where the other one was good...go figure.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000009||Monkeyman||11-03-2001||04:03 AM||||This goes beyond sucking.  I think this has entered the realm of gross negligence.  Just so that nobody thinks I'm  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">ing them, I'll provide the tracking number.  You'll be able to see for yourself where the package originated and where it is now.  Keep in mind where I live.  (Even if you don't know exactly where Wabash is, you know where Indiana is.)<P>The tracking number is:  042096010000181||||reg||1
Z||000010||Monkeyman||11-06-2001||05:57 AM||||<B>UPDATE!!</B><P>According to FedEx, my package is now in Salt Lake City, Utah on it's way to...Columbus, OH (again).  Here we go.  The Columbus, OH hub was where it got "accidentally" shipped to Sacramento in the 1<sup>st</sup> place.  The delivery date is still supposed to be on 8 Nov.  We'll see.  <P>The retarded cust svc rep said that it was "impossible" to know for sure what truck it's on and that FedEx has no communication with the truck drivers.  Umm...I drove a truck for almost 15 years so I know that that's total  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">.  One of the trucking companies that FedEx contracts with is MS Carriers.  I know for a fact that they have satellite communications on all of their trucks.  And "not sure what truck it's on"??  C'mon.  How can you not know what truck a package is on if you're claiming to know where it's going?  What a bunch of idiots.  Maybe my package is lost and they just don't have the kahunas to tell me.<P>I'll keep everyone updated (not that anyone but me cares).||||reg||1
Z||000011||Tigger||11-06-2001||08:54 AM||||FedUp, huh?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">||||reg||7
Z||000012||thomas_l||11-06-2001||09:03 AM||||The only problems I had with FedEx was my own ignorance of customs procedures and a crappy customs broker on a box to Canada some time ago. Also I had a 2 day delay on an overnight envelope because the sender used a south Florida zip code on my address and it floated around in Miami until someone looked one line up and read GEORGIA  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Seems as though you ought to be able to escalate your delay somehow and get that shipment expedited. No gaurantees on Ground shipments but jeez! 2 weeks and counting?||||reg||1
Z||000013||Formula88||11-06-2001||09:23 AM||||I know what you mean.  I ordered a set of KYB shocks and struts for my Formula from Tire Rack.  Instead of shipping them from NJ to NC, they shipped them to New York.  They sat in NY for a few days, then someone decided to put them on a truck for NC.  When they got to the NC hub, they sat there for a few more days before someone tried to deliver them to my apartment.  But, at least they finally arrived.  Looked like they'd been playing handball with the boxes, though. ||||reg||6
Z||000014||88CoupeV6||11-06-2001||11:02 AM||||You guys know what I will say is better. <P>I work for UPS and trust our system. We try to please every customer, which is hard as there is 12-13 million packages/letters shipped in our system each day. :-)  <P>We also care for the USA as we gave 5 million to the disaster relief fund on the 12 of Sept. We also are in partnership with the united way and each employee contributes from there pay.<P>K, nuf bout work  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88coupeV6.jpg">       <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>    <A HREF="http://www.fieropride.com/nefa.htm" TARGET=_blank>Join New England Fiero Association</A>||||reg||7
Z||000015||Monkeyman||11-06-2001||12:05 PM||||Tigger--FedUp.  I like that.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Thomas_l--I've tried and tried to get them to expedite it.  They claim that it's "impossible".   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_bs.gif">  I told them that nothing's impossible.  Some things are just more difficult to do.  They didn't seem to agree with me.  <P>Formula88--If it looks like someone's been playing ball with my package after all this, I'll personally make a trip to Memphis and go ape on them.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>88CoupeV6--I've never had any problems with UPS.  They've never been more than a day late with any of my packages (either sending or receiving).  They've always been my carrier of choice, mostly because of convenience, but now because of this situation.<P>I just spoke with FedUp again.  Now they think that the truck may bypass SLC, Utah.  Why the change?  "Could be it's on a different truck than we originally thought."  So it didn't go to California?  "Sure it did, but we're not exactly sure where it went from there.  According to our computers, it's supposed to be back in Columbus, OH tomorrow."  Umm...yeah, right.  I'll give them another week then assume that it's lost and try to get the sender to file a claim.||||reg||1
Z||000016||Jaygee79||11-06-2001||12:26 PM||||i've always preferred UPS.  never had a problem with them.  they've ALWAYS been right on schedule and I live just about as far out in the boonies as you can get.  Fed Ex and USPS, now I have had too many problems with them to keep track of.<P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="purple">Jaime<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79   ICQ: 85931334</FONT><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/peggy1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Monkeyman||11-06-2001||01:07 PM||||I haven't had many problems with USPS.  They seem to be a little slower than UPS at times.  And UPS will accept larger/heavier packages. ||||reg||1
